      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="always">always</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="never">never</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="at">at</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in">in</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The fictional schedule lists Maya as the one morning receptionist: Maya <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="starts" data-hint="A present-simple routine with the third-person singular subject Maya takes starts." data-fix="Maya starts work at nine every weekday." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> work at nine every weekday. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(present simple)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The attendance log shows Maya arrives before nine on every workday: She is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="always" data-hint="Every workday supports always, and the adverb follows is." data-fix="She is always at the desk before nine." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at the desk before nine. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(adverbs of frequency)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The appointment card gives the exact time 8:30: The appointment is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="at" data-hint="Use at before an exact clock time." data-fix="The appointment is at 8:30." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> 8:30. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(prepositions of time)</span></span></div>
